---
layout: base.njk
---
{#- Climate Code (/work/climate-code/): the sixteen Resilience Stack tools as one explorer. The words
    come from src/_data/climateCode.js; the left column scrolls through them and the map on the right
    follows (src/assets/climate-code/cc.js). Country data is built in climate-30 and synced into
    src/assets/climate-code/data/ by scripts/sync-climate-code.py. The AI notes go through the
    thoughts worker (/climate/ai), which holds the OpenRouter key. -#}
{%- set C = climateCode -%}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/maplibre-gl@4.7.1/dist/maplibre-gl.css" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/climate-code/cc.css?v={{ v }}" />
<div class="cc" data-cc data-kind="intro"
     data-atlas="/assets/climate-code/data/atlas.json?v={{ v }}"
     data-geo="/assets/climate-code/data/countries.geojson?v={{ v }}"
     data-ai="{{ site.thoughtsApi }}/climate/ai">
  <aside class="cc__panel" data-panel aria-label="chapters">
    <div class="cc__bar">
      <ol class="cc__index" data-index aria-label="chapters">
        <li><a href="#top" data-go="top" title="climate code">00</a></li>
        {%- for c in C.chapters %}
        <li><a href="#{{ c.id }}" data-go="{{ c.id }}" title="{{ c.name }}">{{ c.n }}</a></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
      <div class="cc__pick cc__pick--country">
        <label for="cc-country">(country)</label>
        <select id="cc-country" data-country></select>
      </div>
      <form class="cc__pick cc__pick--place" data-place-form autocomplete="off">
        <label for="cc-place">(place)</label>
        <input id="cc-place" name="q" type="search" placeholder="search a town or city" data-place-input />
        <span class="cc__placename" data-place-name></span>
        <ul class="cc__hits" data-place-hits hidden></ul>
      </form>
    </div>

    <header class="cc-ch cc-ch--intro" id="top" data-ch="top" data-kind="intro">
      <p class="cc-ch__lbl">(selected work · 2026)</p>
      <h1 class="cc-ch__title">{{ C.title }}</h1>
      <p class="cc-ch__q">{{ C.question }}</p>
      <p class="cc-ch__text">{{ C.lead }}</p>
      <dl class="cc-meta">
        <div><dt>(role)</dt><dd>{{ role }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>(method)</dt><dd>sixteen streamlit tools · a 150 m city grid · one static explorer</dd></div>
        <div><dt>(data)</dt><dd>world bank · nasa · open-meteo · copernicus · openstreetmap · srtm · meta hrsl · ipcc ar6</dd></div>
        <div><dt>(source)</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/raghavk31/resilience-stack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">resilience-stack &rarr;</a></dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="cc-ch__how">{{ C.how }} <span class="cc-ch__down" aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></p>
    </header>

    {%- for c in C.chapters %}
    <section class="cc-ch cc-ch--{{ c.kind }}{% if c.act %} cc-ch--act{% endif %}" id="{{ c.id }}" data-ch="{{ c.id }}" data-kind="{{ c.kind }}">
      {%- if c.act %}<p class="cc-ch__act">({{ c.act }})</p>{% endif %}
      <p class="cc-ch__lbl">({{ c.n }}) {{ c.name }} <span>· {% if c.day %}day {{ c.day }}{% else %}{{ c.tag }}{% endif %}</span></p>
      <h2 class="cc-ch__q">{{ c.q }}</h2>
      <p class="cc-ch__text">{{ c.text }}</p>
      <div class="cc-ch__ctl" data-ctl></div>
      <div class="cc-ch__body" data-body></div>
      <p class="cc-ch__src" data-src></p>
      {%- if c.data %}
      {%- if c.data.proxy %}<p class="cc-proxy"><span>(proxy)</span> {{ c.data.proxy }}</p>{% endif %}
      <dl class="cc-conf" aria-label="what these numbers rest on">
        <div><dt>(resolution)</dt><dd>{{ c.data.res }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>(date)</dt><dd>{{ c.data.date }}</dd></div>
        {%- for k in ["measured", "modelled", "assumed"] %}{% if c.data[k] %}
        <div class="cc-conf--{{ k }}"><dt>({{ k }})</dt><dd>{{ c.data[k] }}</dd></div>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
      </dl>
      {%- endif %}
    </section>
    {%- endfor %}

    <footer class="cc-ch cc-ch--end" data-ch="end" data-kind="end">
      <p class="cc-ch__lbl">(method)</p>
      {#- COPY: the CityScope sentence was drafted 2026-10-25 for him to edit. -#}
      <p class="cc-ch__text">Each chapter is one of the sixteen tools of the Resilience Stack, built as a Streamlit app in May and June 2026. The country layers are rebuilt ahead of time by <code>explorer/build_atlas.py</code>, which reads each day's own tables and repeats its own formula; the city and place chapters run in your browser against the same live services the apps used. The city grid reads OpenStreetMap from OpenFreeMap's vector tiles, the same tiles the basemap draws. Every city layer is drawn one square tile a cell, after the tile grid of MIT City Science's CityScope, whose reading of a district by density, diversity and proximity the chapters follow. Over it lie sheets of the city's systems, stacked as Ian McHarg stacked them in Design with Nature: the ground and its valleys, the water, the streets as space syntax reads them, roads and rail. The square moves and resizes, after Morphocode's Explorer. The AI notes are written by Claude through OpenRouter.</p>
      <p class="cc-ch__src" data-built></p>
      <noscript><p class="cc-ch__text">The map and the tools on this page are drawn in the browser and need JavaScript.</p></noscript>
    </footer>
  </aside>

  <div class="cc__map" data-map role="region" aria-label="map">
    <div class="cc__legend" data-legend aria-live="polite"></div>
    <details class="cc-layers" data-layers hidden><summary>(layers)</summary><ul></ul></details>
    <div class="cc__tip" data-tip hidden></div>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/maplibre-gl@4.7.1/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
<script type="module" src="/assets/climate-code/cc.js?v={{ v }}"></script>
